=A. Fair laws must be understandable and visible to the people.#Correct. This captures the main idea. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~B. Rules should be hidden from citizens.#The passage argues against hidden rules. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~C. A fair city should have no laws.#The passage supports visible laws. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. Traps are useful civic tools.#Trap is a negative metaphor. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
}

